= Domain Name System — Simple =

The Domain Name System (DNS) is a distributed hierarchical naming system that maps domain names to resource records used by Internet applications.

DNS lets applications resolve human-meaningful names into information such as IP addresses, mail-routing data, service records, and other typed records. Its namespace is hierarchical and delegated across administrative zones.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* DNS ≠ World Wide Web
* domain name ≠ URI

